// WolOS zellij defaults (ADR 0032 "Console" and "Sessions"). zellij reads /etc/zellij/config.kdl when
// you have no ~/.config/zellij/config.kdl; yours replaces this file entirely. Upgrades replace it.
// Sessions are serialized so a named session comes back after a reboot (`wol sessions restore`
// runs `zellij attach --create <name>`). The theme colours come from `wol theme`
// (~/.config/wolos/toolkits/zellij/theme.kdl, theme "wolos"); WolOS passes them when it starts
// zellij for you.
session_serialization true
serialize_pane_viewport true
scroll_buffer_size 50000
pane_frames false
default_layout "compact"
copy_on_select true
mouse_mode true
show_startup_tips false
show_release_notes false
